=============================================================================
SPDK porting checklist
=============================================================================
1. CB-sorted compactor queue: SPDK side must expose an ordered iterator
   (max→min by CB score) over candidate segments — equivalent to
   heap_.ordered_begin()..ordered_end() in cache_sim. The scan is read-only.

2. EWMA (or MovingAverage) ratios for {compaction_ratio,
   compaction_ratio_in_ghost_cache, eviction_ratio, eviction_ratio_in_ghost_cache}.
   GS best with half-life ≈ DEFAULT × 0.25 (= 1.57M blocks in our tests,
   = ~1.5 segments worth of host writes). EWMA must accept cumulative-counter
   updates ("updateFromCumulative(ts, cum_count)") to allow rate extraction
   from monotonic counters.

3. util_step_ (θ): hill-climb increment for target_valid_blk_rate. 0.02 in
   our experiments; smaller = finer control, larger = faster reaction.

4. periodic_ratio_ (r): flush-vs-compact weight in the trade-off; r·Δflush
   > Δcomp ⇒ raise target. Pick per workload/QoS target.

5. State plumbing: 4 new fields (ghost_compacted_blocks_sum_,
   last_ghost_sum_ts_, ghost_sum_initialized_, last_invalidate_at_comp_)
   live on the cache instance; reset on cache init.

6. invalidate_blocks counter: monotonic count of host pages invalidated
   inside the log cache (overwrite/discard). SPDK side typically already
   tracks this; just expose it for the per-comp window i estimate.

7. timestamp: monotonic host-page-write counter (1 per page). Used for
   dt in ghost_compacted_blocks_sum_ accumulation and for periodic-tick
   modular gating (segment_size_blocks/4, segment_size_blocks*8).

=============================================================================
Notes on correctness
=============================================================================
- First real compaction: dt is undefined ⇒ skip rate accumulation, just
  anchor last_ghost_sum_ts_ + last_invalidate_at_comp_. Without this guard
  the first tick spikes ghost_compacted_blocks_sum_ by a huge dt × rate.

- inv_corr factor 1/(1 - θ·i): θ·i is bounded to 0.95 to avoid blowup
  when both util_step and i are pathologically large. In practice θ=0.02,
  i ≤ 1.0 ⇒ correction ≤ 1.02, i.e. negligible. The factor is kept for
  derivation honesty (free-space target accounts for in-flight overwrite).

- u_avg/(1-u_avg) is the classical Greedy-WAF cost per host page. The
  cumulative form (Σ v / Σ inv) is the natural generalization across the
  m segments needed to reclaim θ·N·seg free space — equivalent to the
  per-epoch view that one θ-epoch reclaims θ·N·seg pages and consumes
  Σ v_i compaction work.
